IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), s 4: maximum yearly insurable earnings.
-- Written by the keel agent (ei-g0).
-- The formula needs Statistics Canada's Average Weekly Earnings, which are published outside the text.
-- So the rules below take the two 12-month averages as inputs, and every other piece takes "the maximum
-- yearly insurable earnings for the year" as a plain NUMBER input (the figure Service Canada publishes
-- for that year). This module writes down no published figure: the amounts in its tests are illustrative.
-- The pieces that read the figure are those of the sections s 4(1) names: 14(1.1), 17, 82(2), 95, 145.

§ `Section 4(5) - Average Weekly Earnings`

-- src:78 | (a) the average for the 12-month period ending on April 30 in the preceding year of the Average Weekly Earnings for each month in that period
-- src:86 | (5) The Average Weekly Earnings for a month is the average weekly earnings of the Industrial Aggregate in Canada for the month as published by Statistics Canada under the authority of the Statistics Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 4(2)(a), s 4(5) (src:78) (src:86)
GIVEN months IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 4(2)(a) the average of the Average Weekly Earnings for each month of a 12-month period` IS
    IF count months EQUALS 12
    THEN JUST (sum months DIVIDED BY 12)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:78 | (a) the average for the 12-month period ending on April 30 in the preceding year of the Average Weekly Earnings for each month in that period
-- src:80 | (b) the ratio that the average for the 12-month period ending on April 30 in that preceding year of the Average Weekly Earnings for each month in that 12-month period bears to the average for the 12-month period ending 12 months prior to April 30 of that preceding year of the Average Weekly Earnings for each month in that 12-month period ending 12 months prior to April 30 of that preceding year.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 4(2)(a), s 4(2)(b) (src:78) (src:80)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Period of days`
DECIDE `s 4(2)(a) the 12-month period ending on April 30 in the preceding year` IS
    `Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay (year MINUS 2) 5 1), (YearMonthDay (year MINUS 1) 4 30)

-- src:80 | (b) the ratio that the average for the 12-month period ending on April 30 in that preceding year of the Average Weekly Earnings for each month in that 12-month period bears to the average for the 12-month period ending 12 months prior to April 30 of that preceding year of the Average Weekly Earnings for each month in that 12-month period ending 12 months prior to April 30 of that preceding year.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 4(2)(b) (src:80)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Period of days`
DECIDE `s 4(2)(b) the 12-month period ending 12 months prior to April 30 of that preceding year` IS
    `Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay (year MINUS 3) 5 1), (YearMonthDay (year MINUS 2) 4 30)

§ `Section 4(1) to (4) - the amount`

-- src:75 | 4 (1) For the purposes of subsection 14(1.1), section 17, subsection 82(2) and sections 95 and 145, the maximum yearly insurable earnings is $39,000 until the amount calculated in accordance with subsection (2) for a year, before rounding down under subsection (4), exceeds $39,000, in which case the maximum yearly insurable earnings for that year is that amount, rounded down under subsection (4).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 4(1) (src:75)
`s 4(1) base amount of the maximum yearly insurable earnings` MEANS 39000

-- "52 times the product obtained by multiplying (a) the average ... by (b) the ratio that [that average]
-- bears to the average for the 12-month period ending 12 months prior". A is the first average, B the second.
-- src:77 | (2) The amount referred to in subsection (1) is the amount equal to 52 times the product obtained by multiplying
-- src:78 | (a) the average for the 12-month period ending on April 30 in the preceding year of the Average Weekly Earnings for each month in that period
-- src:79 | by
-- src:80 | (b) the ratio that the average for the 12-month period ending on April 30 in that preceding year of the Average Weekly Earnings for each month in that 12-month period bears to the average for the 12-month period ending 12 months prior to April 30 of that preceding year of the Average Weekly Earnings for each month in that 12-month period ending 12 months prior to April 30 of that preceding year.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 4(2) (src:77-80)
GIVEN `the average for the 12-month period ending on April 30 in the preceding year` IS A NUMBER
      `the average for the 12-month period ending 12 months prior to that April 30` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 4(2) the amount calculated in accordance with subsection (2)` IS
    52 TIMES (`the average for the 12-month period ending on April 30 in the preceding year` TIMES (`the average for the 12-month period ending on April 30 in the preceding year` DIVIDED BY `the average for the 12-month period ending 12 months prior to that April 30`))

-- src:82 | (3) For years subsequent to the year in which the maximum yearly insurable earnings exceeds $39,000, before rounding down under subsection (4), the maximum yearly insurable earnings is the maximum yearly insurable earnings for the preceding year, before rounding down under that subsection, multiplied by the ratio that the average for the 12-month period ending on April 30 in that preceding year of the Average Weekly Earnings for each month in that 12-month period bears to the average for the 12-month period ending 12 months prior to April 30 of that preceding year of the Average Weekly Earnings for each month in that 12-month period ending 12 months prior to April 30 of that preceding year.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 4(3) (src:82)
GIVEN `the maximum yearly insurable earnings for the preceding year, before rounding down` IS A NUMBER
      `the average for the 12-month period ending on April 30 in the preceding year` IS A NUMBER
      `the average for the 12-month period ending 12 months prior to that April 30` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 4(3) the amount calculated in accordance with subsection (3)` IS
    `the maximum yearly insurable earnings for the preceding year, before rounding down` TIMES (`the average for the 12-month period ending on April 30 in the preceding year` DIVIDED BY `the average for the 12-month period ending 12 months prior to that April 30`)

-- src:84 | (4) If the amount calculated in accordance with subsection (2) or (3) is not a multiple of one hundred dollars, the amount of the maximum yearly insurable earnings is rounded down to the nearest multiple of one hundred dollars.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 4(4) (src:84)
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 4(4) the amount rounded down to the nearest multiple of one hundred dollars` IS
    100 TIMES FLOOR (amount DIVIDED BY 100)

§ `Section 4(1) and (3) - the year`

-- The first input says whether an earlier year has already exceeded the base amount: JUST that year's
-- amount before rounding down, or NOTHING if no year has yet. The text presupposes positive published
-- earnings, so an average that is not above zero gets NOTHING, never a number.
-- Assumed, not ruled: s 4(3) has no floor. Once a year has exceeded $39,000, a later year is the earlier
-- year's amount times the ratio, even if that comes out below $39,000 (see NOTES.md, Fork register).
-- src:75 | 4 (1) For the purposes of subsection 14(1.1), section 17, subsection 82(2) and sections 95 and 145, the maximum yearly insurable earnings is $39,000 until the amount calculated in accordance with subsection (2) for a year, before rounding down under subsection (4), exceeds $39,000, in which case the maximum yearly insurable earnings for that year is that amount, rounded down under subsection (4).
-- src:82 | (3) For years subsequent to the year in which the maximum yearly insurable earnings exceeds $39,000, before rounding down under subsection (4), the maximum yearly insurable earnings is the maximum yearly insurable earnings for the preceding year, before rounding down under that subsection, multiplied by the ratio that the average for the 12-month period ending on April 30 in that preceding year of the Average Weekly Earnings for each month in that 12-month period bears to the average for the 12-month period ending 12 months prior to April 30 of that preceding year of the Average Weekly Earnings for each month in that 12-month period ending 12 months prior to April 30 of that preceding year.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 4(1), s 4(3) (src:75) (src:82)
GIVEN `the preceding year's amount before rounding down, if an earlier year has exceeded $39,000` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the average for the 12-month period ending on April 30 in the preceding year` IS A NUMBER
      `the average for the 12-month period ending 12 months prior to that April 30` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 4(1) the maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year, before rounding down` IS
    IF `the average for the 12-month period ending on April 30 in the preceding year` AT MOST 0 OR `the average for the 12-month period ending 12 months prior to that April 30` AT MOST 0
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `the preceding year's amount before rounding down, if an earlier year has exceeded $39,000`
         WHEN JUST earlier THEN JUST (`s 4(3) the amount calculated in accordance with subsection (3)` earlier `the average for the 12-month period ending on April 30 in the preceding year` `the average for the 12-month period ending 12 months prior to that April 30`)
         WHEN NOTHING THEN
            IF `s 4(2) the amount calculated in accordance with subsection (2)` `the average for the 12-month period ending on April 30 in the preceding year` `the average for the 12-month period ending 12 months prior to that April 30` GREATER THAN `s 4(1) base amount of the maximum yearly insurable earnings`
            THEN JUST (`s 4(2) the amount calculated in accordance with subsection (2)` `the average for the 12-month period ending on April 30 in the preceding year` `the average for the 12-month period ending 12 months prior to that April 30`)
            ELSE JUST (`s 4(1) base amount of the maximum yearly insurable earnings`)

-- src:75 | 4 (1) For the purposes of subsection 14(1.1), section 17, subsection 82(2) and sections 95 and 145, the maximum yearly insurable earnings is $39,000 until the amount calculated in accordance with subsection (2) for a year, before rounding down under subsection (4), exceeds $39,000, in which case the maximum yearly insurable earnings for that year is that amount, rounded down under subsection (4).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 4(1) (src:75)
GIVEN `the preceding year's amount before rounding down, if an earlier year has exceeded $39,000` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the average for the 12-month period ending on April 30 in the preceding year` IS A NUMBER
      `the average for the 12-month period ending 12 months prior to that April 30` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 4(1) the maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year` IS
    CONSIDER `s 4(1) the maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year, before rounding down` `the preceding year's amount before rounding down, if an earlier year has exceeded $39,000` `the average for the 12-month period ending on April 30 in the preceding year` `the average for the 12-month period ending 12 months prior to that April 30`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST unrounded THEN JUST (`s 4(4) the amount rounded down to the nearest multiple of one hundred dollars` unrounded)

-- What the following year takes as its first input: this year's amount before rounding down once some
-- year has exceeded $39,000, and NOTHING while every year so far has been at the base amount.
-- src:82 | (3) For years subsequent to the year in which the maximum yearly insurable earnings exceeds $39,000, before rounding down under subsection (4), the maximum yearly insurable earnings is the maximum yearly insurable earnings for the preceding year, before rounding down under that subsection, multiplied by the ratio that the average for the 12-month period ending on April 30 in that preceding year of the Average Weekly Earnings for each month in that 12-month period bears to the average for the 12-month period ending 12 months prior to April 30 of that preceding year of the Average Weekly Earnings for each month in that 12-month period ending 12 months prior to April 30 of that preceding year.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 4(3) (src:82)
GIVEN `the preceding year's amount before rounding down, if an earlier year has exceeded $39,000` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the average for the 12-month period ending on April 30 in the preceding year` IS A NUMBER
      `the average for the 12-month period ending 12 months prior to that April 30` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 4(3) the amount to carry into the following year` IS
    CONSIDER `the preceding year's amount before rounding down, if an earlier year has exceeded $39,000`
    WHEN JUST earlier THEN `s 4(1) the maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year, before rounding down` (JUST earlier) `the average for the 12-month period ending on April 30 in the preceding year` `the average for the 12-month period ending 12 months prior to that April 30`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        CONSIDER `s 4(1) the maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year, before rounding down` NOTHING `the average for the 12-month period ending on April 30 in the preceding year` `the average for the 12-month period ending 12 months prior to that April 30`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST unrounded THEN
            IF unrounded GREATER THAN `s 4(1) base amount of the maximum yearly insurable earnings`
            THEN JUST unrounded
            ELSE NOTHING
